<p>The Pentagon has identified four U.S. Army Reserve soldiers killed March 1 after a drone attack hit a command center/commercial port area in Kuwait, as the U.S.-Iran conflict continues to widen; U.S. Central Command and the Pentagon said six Americans died in the attack. The four soldiers were assigned to the 103rd Sustainment Command (based in Des Moines, Iowa) and worked in logistics—roles that keep units supplied with essentials like food and equipment.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hT0FCP03mgwPj1qj9oYmH8IwCCjI9mpd6EFKlfBPYFfHYqG0y9s5AVDJCm1VdmIv7S5MV4JpOqysHLPzNWeA9ezu6OEH9tug3CpCI1b4NeIbbtL2EIBcVgtOp93ya_BPoChOEXNFptkM7JPVeJLJU65DyQqKY-ynpnLyvGKYWQSLIePnqqXbV142vbq2lVOgpkOT0nnYkS0dCsqAdD1oDzpib96vwX4A3FfSUL3yEsP9wTipJGokaxQJloc24YpylhO-1VhhuVN52g-5-Q' alt='This photo provided by Andrew Coady shows his son, Declan Coady, on his graduation day at Fort Sill in March 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ages 20 to 42: The service members identified so far ranged in age from 20 to 42.</li><li>Investigation ongoing: The Pentagon said the March 1 deaths happened during an “unmanned aircraft system attack,” and said the incident is still under investigation.</li><li>Remembered at home: Relatives and coverage described some of the soldiers as devoted parents and long-serving reservists, a reminder that the war’s toll extends beyond the front lines.</li><li>Evacuation effort: With the fighting spilling into neighboring countries and unsettling markets, U.S. officials said they are looking at more ways to help Americans leave, including adding flight options and weighing land routes.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon/U.S. Central Command: The U.S. military said a drone attack in Kuwait killed the service members, and said it would release identities as families were notified; the Pentagon said the fallen were Army Reserve logistics soldiers from different states. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/names-us-service-members-killed-iran-war-kuwait/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>U.S. State Department (Marco Rubio): Rubio said about 9,000 Americans had left the region and roughly 1,500 still wanted to depart, with officials working to expand options. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-03-0800/middle-east-us-iran-war-live-updates-pentagon-identifies-us-soldiers-killed-kuwait-strike'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump offered condolences to the families and said the U.S. would “avenge their deaths,” while warning that more casualties were possible. (<a href='https://time.com/7382451/iran-war-us-deaths-soldiers-kuwait-amor-coady-khork-tietjens/'>TIME</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-03-0800/middle-east-us-iran-war-live-updates-pentagon-identifies-us-soldiers-killed-kuwait-strike'>US-Iran war live updates: Pentagon identifies US soldiers killed in Kuwait strike</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq33ynl07o'>First US soldiers to die in Iran conflict are identified</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-four-of-six-us-soldiers-killed-in-iran-retaliation-identified/'>Four of six U.S. soldiers killed in Iran retaliation identified</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/names-us-service-members-killed-iran-war-kuwait/'>Pentagon releases names of first U.S. service members killed in Iran war</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7382451/iran-war-us-deaths-soldiers-kuwait-amor-coady-khork-tietjens/'>U.S. Identifies Four U.S. Troops Killed in Iran War: What to Know</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/pentagon-identifies-4-of-6-u-s-soldiers-killed-in-iran-war-by-drone-strike-in-kuwait'>Pentagon identifies 4 of 6 U.S. soldiers killed in Iran war by drone strike in Kuwait</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>